  "scope": "Optional primary-raster RG8 material normal pages through retained native terrain residency; cube-sphere metric correction, surface-gradient mip/residency blending, resolved disable/filter tiers, explicit water isolation. Reference algorithm/license review in doc 69. No simulation, authoritative heights, topology, contacts or secondary-ray normal changes; not visual acceptance or Bevy retirement.",
  "contract": {
    "producer": "worldgen-rocky::lod::build_gpu_material_page_with_normals and appearance::surface_normal_grain_height; land-only filtered Perlin bands 8/4/2/1/0.5 m plus 32/128/512 m, independent of authoritative height.",
    "metric": "Two physical cube-sphere direction chords and grain differences solved in the orthonormal face tangent frame; same-face level-16 horizontal/vertical apron derivatives agree at shared edges.",
    "representation": "128x128 linear RG8 unit-normal XY, positive z reconstructed, eight mips. CPU mips and page hierarchy average decoded XY/z gradients; texture hardware interpolates unit XY within/across mips (approximation). z floor 0.01 for extreme/invalid input. No universal grazing/filtered-normal error bound.",
    "residency": "Normal array and sparse normal-bearing directory reuse the albedo layer slots and generations. Missing coverage contributes flat without normalization. Globe transition and coarse/fine LOD follow albedo.",
    "consumers": "Primary regular/conforming terrain direct diffuse and land direct/environment GGX. Water classifier suppresses this perturbation; water wave normals, shadow receiver plane, emissive geographic night gating and physical geometry stay independent. Bevy binds the existing array and one empty directory; secondary paths remain flat.",
    "settings": "renderer.terrain_normal_maps=false skips native grain/normal mip generation, normal uploads, full array and shader sampling. Only 1x1 dummy texture/one 16-byte directory entry remain. Restart required. surface_quality low/medium/high uses +2/+1/+0 normal mip bias. Native capture now includes the existing common resolved metadata map.",
